  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The capacity of the institutions for the prevention and resolution of labour disputes in Lesotho has been strengthened, through the adoption of measures included in a tripartite action plan based on results of the self-assessment diagnostic tool on effectiveness of labour dispute prevention and resolution institution. For example, by improving the conciliation and arbitration skills of conciliators and arbitrators; enhancement of their analytical skills of evidence and arbitration award writing; and use of social platforms to inform the users of the system on the services provided by the institutions. These measures have improved the capacity of institutions to respond to the demand for the provision of their conflict resolution services. In August 2022, the ILO facilitated the implementation of the self-assessment diagnostic tool for the effectiveness of labour dispute prevention and resolution institutions, namely, the Directorate of Dispute Prevention and Resolution  the Labour Court. As a result of this intervention, a costed action plan was adopted by the tripartite Industrial Relations Council to generate improvement measures.</narrative>
   </description>
