  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.2. Increased capacity of Member States to ensure safe and healthy working conditions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The national tripartite committee on OSH (NACOSH) developed the implementation plan and M&amp;E framework for the OSH policy, as part of the operationalization of the national OSH policy. The implementation has commenced and so far achieved the sensitization and capacitation of tripartite partners and key stakeholders on application of the key OSH conventions, the ratification of C187, and the development of the comprehensive and gender-responsive OSH Bill, one of the policy implementation strategies,  (still to be presented to cabinet) as outputs towards expanding the scope or reinforcing an existing infrastructure with a mandate on safety and health at work.  
The successful implementation of the national OSH policy will benefit the national competent authorities including the inspectorates through reinforced mandates and enhanced capacities, as well as the workers and enterprises including workers in informal sector, and other workers in situations of vulnerability, through extended protection and reduction of occupational injuries and diseases. During the biennium, the ILO provided technical support towards build-up activities that led to the reported results, including:
&#x2022; provided technical assistance in developing national OSH situational analysis and based on the analysis provided recommendations to the country to implement national policy on OSH and ratify ILO Convention 187. 
&#x2022; capacitation of the tripartite National  Advisory Committee on OSH (NACOSH) to be able to oversee the implementation of the above.
&#x2022; development of the gender-responsive national OSH Bill, 
&#x2022; compilation of the legal gap analysis against C155 and C187 to inform the development of the OSH Bill,
&#x2022; development of the OSH Bill, and
&#x2022; sensitization of tripartite constitutes and key stakeholders ton key ILO Conventions C155 and C187.
The ILO also provided technical and financial support towards the development of the implementation plan and M&amp;E Framework for the national OSH Policy.</narrative>
   </description>
